If `allow_alias = true` is set but **all enum values have distinct numbers**, the enum is **invalid**: enabling aliases requires that at least two enum values share a number.

The validator reports an error equivalent to:

> “enum allows aliases, but none were found”

To use `allow_alias`, define at least one alias pair, for example:

```proto
enum Example {
  option allow_alias = true;
  FIRST = 0;
  SECOND = 1;
  SECOND_ALIAS = 1;
}
```
